The Argon2id CUDA engine (gpu/bnt_gpu.cu) and the reference code (src/argon_ref.h,
written from RFC 9106 / RFC 7693) are original work.
The pool protocol follows the stratum of bntpool.com as implemented by the seine miner
(github.com/zpalmtree/seine, BSD-3-Clause); no seine code is included.
Correctness references used for the tests only (not linked into the miner):
  - the Rust argon2 0.5 crate (RustCrypto), called exactly like Blocknet core
    (github.com/blocknetprivacy/core, crypto-rs/src/pow.rs): tools/bntref -> tests/vectors.txt.
The stratum client (json.h, tls_conn.*) comes from FiloMiner / NullMiner (same author, Apache-2.0).

The Windows release zip also contains third-party components (not in this repository):
  - OpenSSL (Apache-2.0), statically linked into bntminer.exe (MSYS2 MINGW64 package);
  - the MinGW-w64 runtime, winpthreads and libstdc++/libgcc (permissive licences, GCC
    Runtime Library Exception), statically linked into bntminer.exe;
  - cudart64_12.dll, the NVIDIA CUDA runtime, redistributed under the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit
    EULA (used by bgpu.dll);
  - vcruntime140.dll, vcruntime140_1.dll, msvcp140.dll, the Microsoft Visual C++ 2015-2022
    runtime (redistributable under the Visual Studio licence terms, used by bgpu.dll);
  - ca-bundle.crt, the Mozilla CA certificate bundle (MPL-2.0), from MSYS2.
